MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The O-ring assortment and wing nuts fit my habit of keeping useful repair hardware on hand: replacement seals and hand-tightened fasteners add capabilities alongside my existing kits.",
    "The gap-filling adhesive feels useful because it offers a way to repair parts where my tapes, rivets, and bolts may be awkward to use."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Both filament recommendations assume I have a printing project or printer supplies to replenish, which my recent interactions do not establish.",
    "The cleanroom wipes and bathroom sealant serve specific jobs I do not currently have, while the long half-inch bolts require a particular fit that general interest in hardware does not establish."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in tools and fabrication seems to have been stretched into interest in any making supplies, including decorative printing filament.",
    "My purchases of fastener assortments seem to have been taken as a reason to offer any fastener, even a narrowly sized refill or unusually large bolt."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "I often choose assortments that prepare me for several repair needs; a single-size rivet refill is less useful until I know which size I am running short of.",
    "I care about what an item adds to the supplies I already have: gap filling gives me a clearer reason to choose an adhesive than another general-purpose glue."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my repair and fastening interests but sometimes confused broadly related supplies with useful additions for my current work."
}
